**Usage:**

```tsx
// Default fallback
<ErrorBoundary>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>

// Custom fallback
<ErrorBoundary fallback={(error, reset) => (
  <div>
    <p>{error.message}</p>
    <button onClick={reset}>Retry</button>
  </div>
)}>
  <MyComponent />
</ErrorBoundary>
```

Key points:
- `getDerivedStateFromError` captures the error into state (triggers fallback render)
- `componentDidCatch` logs message + both stack traces to console
- `reset()` clears state so children re-mount fresh on retry
- Custom `fallback` prop overrides default UI; default UI works with zero config
